    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and it passes along with the full build.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required the owner response to include an `initials` field \u2014 the upper-cased first letters of `firstName` and `lastName`, dot-separated with a trailing dot (e.g. `J.S.`).\n\nTwo changes, following the project's generated-DTO + MapStruct pattern (the same way the existing `displayName` field is handled):\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `initials` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping` expression on `toOwnerDto` computing the initials:\n   ```java\n   Character.toUpperCase(owner.getFirstName().charAt(0)) + \".\" +\n   Character.toUpperCase(owner.getLastName().charAt(0)) + \".\"\n   ```\n\n`Character.toUpperCase(char)` returns a `char`, so it concatenates as the letter (not a numeric code). The `GET /api/owners/{id}` pipeline already responds via `RespondWithOwner` \u2192 `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto`, so no wiring changes were needed.\n\nTest results: `AcceptanceTest` (including the new `coreComputesInitials` \u2014 `john`/`smith` \u2192 `J.S.`) passes, and the full `./mvnw test` build is green.",
